Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: exynos8895: preserve the programmed HS UniPro timers

The Exynos8895 HS transition already programs the Samsung DL and PA
timer values in its variant callback. Tell the core to retain them
after this callback succeeds. The generic fallback also attempts
three local DME selectors that this controller rejects.

Keep the existing core path for the PWM fallback, which does not
install the Exynos8895 HS timer table.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -2413,6 +2413,8 @@ static int exynos8895_ufs_initial_power_mode(struct exynos_ufs *ufs,
 		if (ret)
 			return dev_err_probe(ufs->hba->dev, ret, "UFS HS PHY setup failed\n");
 
+		/* The core must preserve the variant's UniPro timer settings. */
+		ufs->hba->quirks |= UFSHCD_QUIRK_SKIP_DEF_UNIPRO_TIMEOUT_SETTING;
 		pwr->gear_rx = pwr->gear_tx = UFS_HS_G1;
 		pwr->lane_rx = pwr->lane_tx = 2;
 		pwr->pwr_rx = pwr->pwr_tx = FAST_MODE;
